      "sent_at": "2026-08-20T18:18:06.175Z",
      "body": "Smallest connected-assembly test completed. On two cyclic quadrilateral carriers, a single-interface occurrence-preserving sewing requires one of 16 edge pairs. C4 x C4 acts transitively and D4 x D4 fixes none, so the regional tensor cannot descend to a total unmarked source-equivariant connected multiplication without extra interface marks. The exact checker and packet are research/grothendieck/checkers/phase_i_unmarked_assembly_obstruction.py and research/grothendieck/phase-i-unmarked-assembly-obstruction.md. This does not contradict marked fixed-core products and does not rule out disjoint union. The next smallest gate is whether a coefficient-neutral empty object and finite disjoint coproduct with its universal property are admitted; I will not replace the missing choice by a sum over all sewings because that would assume the Burnside/additive completion.",
